{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 5891532029699363520, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 638, "mtime": 1791871732.1640317, "sha256": "514fb3ca03e8f709dacd8f29d5e33f083d38b7bf9b75acea5c2701d99b60aee8"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 634, "mtime": 1791871736.236355, "sha256": "97d6c5c974678048d2c603c38067b35779e30efb4b1d87acbbb5428fb98ac829"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/6/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/6/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running it before and after the fix.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** in binary, `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so Python's built-in `round()` rounds it down. `round()` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit (`0.125` \u2192 `0.12`), which isn't the half-up behaviour the docstring promises.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now rounds the float's shortest printed form (`repr(x)`, here `\"2.675\"`) with `Decimal.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)`, then converts back to `float`, so callers get the same type as before. `add_vat` uses `round_money`, so it gets the fix too. Negative halves now round away from zero: `-2.675` \u2192 `-2.68`.\n\n**Verification:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`. Its tie cases (`2.675`, `1.005`, `0.125`, `-2.675`) fail with the old `round()`, which gives `2.67 1.0 0.12 -2.67`, and they pass now. The new tests and the existing `tests/test_split.py` pass. pytest isn't installed here, so I called the test functions directly with `python3`.\n\nOne more problem I noticed but didn't change, since it's outside this fix: `split()` uses `int(total * 100)`, which cuts off values that sit just below a whole cent in binary. For example, `0.29 * 100` is `28.999\u2026`, so it becomes `28`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 248882, "requests_cache_write": 13131, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1628114, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2365, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial6", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 11, "score": 1.0, "started_a